WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.633
Reflection.

2
00:00:01.933 --> 00:00:07.100
Two extra model calls, no new tools, no new data, and noticeably better answers.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.167
Reflection is a second pass where the model critiques its own draft.

4
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:13.533
First, a draft.

5
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.933
Then a critique, whose only job is to find flaws.

6
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:19.867
Then a revision that fixes every flaw it found.

7
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.100
Why does it work?

8
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.167
Critiquing is an easier task than generating.

9
00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:33.000
Reading a draft for flaws needs less juggling of constraints than writing one, so the same model does better as its own reviewer.

10
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.767
Let's watch the three roles.

11
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:37.733
The first call writes a draft.

12
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.667
The draft says soon, with a distance in miles.

13
00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:43.400
The second call is a separate harsh reviewer.

14
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.502
It spots the missing date and the mixed units.

15
00:00:46.502 --> 00:00:53.567
Keep roles in separate calls, because asking for a great, self-checked answer in one call loses most of the benefit.

16
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.600
In code, it is just three calls.

17
00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.467
One call drafts the answer.

18
00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.467
A second call lists flaws, and only flaws.

19
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:05.833
And a third rewrites the answer with both the draft and the flaws in view.

20
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.900
Now the evidence from the Orbital Research Agent.

21
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:16.067
Scoring ten hazard summaries against a checklist, only four were clean without reflection.

22
00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.305
With it, nine were.

23
00:01:17.305 --> 00:01:20.825
The critique reliably flagged that soon is not a date.

24
00:01:20.825 --> 00:01:24.867
Two extra calls per report is the cheapest lift you will find.

25
00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:26.891
Let's recap.

26
00:01:26.891 --> 00:01:29.500
Reflection is draft, critique, revise.

27
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.033
Critiquing is easier than generating.

28
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:34.033
Keep each role in its own call.

29
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:36.438
And always measure with and without.

30
00:01:36.438 --> 00:01:37.900
Next up: self-correction.
